@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowColor #6C83AD
skinparam classBackgroundColor #F4F7FE
skinparam classBorderColor #9BAFD4
skinparam actorBorderColor #6C83AD
skinparam usecaseBackgroundColor #F4F7FE
skinparam usecaseBorderColor #9BAFD4
title Incident lifecycle — state and permission checks
start
:Employee reports incident;
:NEW;
:Classify selected category and service;
:CLASSIFIED;
:Calculate score, priority and SLA deadlines;
:Detect duplicates / recommend technician;
if (Eligible technician available?) then (yes)
 :Assign technician with capacity lock;
else (no)
 :Remain CLASSIFIED;
 :Administrator assigns when capacity is available;
endif
:ASSIGNED;
:Assigned technician acknowledges;
:ACKNOWLEDGED;
:Start investigation;
:IN_PROGRESS;
repeat
 :Add notes / request and receive information;
 :Record resolution details;
repeat while (Details shorter than 10 characters?) is (yes)
:RESOLVED;
if (Reporter confirms fix?) then (yes)
 :Record verification details;
 :VERIFIED;
 :Reporter closes incident;
 :CLOSED;
else (no)
 :Reporter / assigned technician / administrator provides reopening justification;
 :IN_PROGRESS (reopened);
 :Investigate and repeat resolution + verification;
endif
:Preserve records, feedback and audit history;
stop
note right
 Every action validates role, ownership and current IncidentState.
 Disallowed transitions return HTTP 409 with no committed mutation.
 Unauthorized operations return HTTP 403.
 SLA scheduler independently records warnings, violations and escalations.
 Closed incidents can be reopened with justification and an audit event.
end note

@enduml
